/* book exam traps: Drawing the feed on the dish. The prime-focus feed sits at the focus, a distance f in front of the vertex. | Dropping η or the π. G = η(πD/λ)²: leaving out η = 0.6 adds 2.2 dB; writing (D/λ)² instead of (πD/λ)² is wrong by π², nearly 10 dB. | Mixing units in 70λ/D. λ and D must be in the same unit; the answer is in degrees. | Taking a deeper dish (smaller f/D) as higher gain. f/D sets the feed angle, not the gain; gain comes from D/λ and η. | Placing the Cassegrain subreflector beyond the focus. The hyperbolic Cassegrain subreflector is inside the focus; the ellipsoidal Gregorian one is beyond it. */
